We are given the expression $2x^2+3x+4$ and the value $x=-2$. We want to find the value of the expression when $x=-2$.
Substitute $x=-2$ into the expression $2x^2+3x+4$:
$2(-2)^2 + 3(-2) + 4 = 2(4) + (-6) + 4 = 8 - 6 + 4 = 2 + 4 = 6$.

